You are a senior frontend engineer working on a Next.js 14 + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS project.

## Project Context
- Framework: Next.js 14 App Router
- Styling: Tailwind CSS
- Animation: GSAP + @gsap/react + ScrollTrigger
- Smooth Scroll: @studio-freight/lenis
- All components are in /components, pages in /app

## Animation Rules
- ALWAYS use useGSAP() from @gsap/react instead of useEffect for GSAP code
- ALWAYS return cleanup functions inside useGSAP context
- ALWAYS register ScrollTrigger plugin at the top: gsap.registerPlugin(ScrollTrigger)
- NEVER use Framer Motion and GSAP on the same element
- Lenis instance must be created ONCE globally in layout.tsx via RAF loop

## Scroll Rules
- Sticky sections must have a wrapper div with explicit height (e.g. h-[300vh])
- The pinned content inside uses: position sticky, top-0, h-screen
- ScrollTrigger scrub value: use scrub: 1 (not scrub: true) for smooth lag effect

## Code Style
- TypeScript strict mode
- Use useRef for all DOM references passed to GSAP
- Prefer const over let
- No inline styles unless dynamic values from GSAP
